      statement: "Flags should produce their documented effect on output. Section labels should match the edge semantics of the entries they group. Either the headers partition by edge type, or by direction with documented inclusion semantics."  # 4066
      root_cause: "The explanation subcommand has several distinct quality problems. One subcommand flag intended to surface provenance information produces byte-identical output with or without the flag enabled — the flag is wholly unwired. Separately, the subcommand's section headers conflate edge direction with edge semantics: a \"Calls\" section under a symbol header may contain entries that are not invocations (containment relations, instantiations, references); a \"Called by\" section may contain entries that are class-creation rather than invocation. A consumer reading the section labels infers a relationship that does not match the underlying edge type."  # 4066
